<title>LITHUANIA: 476 NEW CARS SOLD IN APRIL-REPORT.</title>
<headline>476 NEW CARS SOLD IN APRIL-REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were 476 new cars sold in</p>
<p>Lithuania in April, the daily Lietuvos rytas reported on</p>
<p>Thursday.</p>
<p>The newspaper presented the following data on the sales of</p>
<p>new cars:</p>
<p>    Producer/distributor	No of cars    The most popular</p>
<p>							  models</p>
<p>    - LADA (Egzotika/Zemgala) 126(68/58)    21099,21074</p>
<p>    - Volkswagen (Eva Auto)   88		Caddy,Passat</p>
<p>    - Skoda (ARX)		 61		Felicia</p>
<p>    - Opel (Zaibo ratas/	38(16/9/9/4)  Vectra,Omega,</p>
<p>    Autodina/ Armi/ Rasmitas)		   Combo,Astra</p>
<p>    - Ford (Vista Ford)	 23		n/a</p>
<p>    - Hyundai (Vytaras)	 18		Sonata</p>
<p>    - Mazda (Palvita/	   18(12/6)	626</p>
<p>RSS Enterprises)</p>
<p>    - Honda (Honda Centras)   17		Civic</p>
<p>    - Audi (Eva Auto)	   13		A6</p>
<p>    - Nissan (Raitas)	   11		Almera</p>
<p>    - Daewoo			11		Espero</p>
<p>(Stern von Litauen)</p>
<p>The newspaper provided no figures for comparison.</p>
<p>Auto Research, a local marketing research firm, said</p>
<p>earlier that the number of new cars sold during the first three</p>
<p>months of the year was 1,396, excluding ladas.</p>
<p>The company also said that there were 6,017 new cars sold</p>
<p>in 1996, 2,672 Ladas excluded.</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
